# Advisor System Architecture

## Purpose

The Advisor System Architecture defines the major software components that implement the Advisor Intelligence Specification (AIS).

Its purpose is to translate the Advisor's reasoning model into a modular, scalable, and maintainable software architecture.

This document intentionally focuses on responsibilities rather than implementation details.

Future implementation may use different technologies, programming languages, or deployment strategies without altering the architectural principles defined here.

---

## Guiding Principle

Every architectural component should have a single, clearly defined responsibility.

Components should collaborate through well-defined interfaces while remaining independently testable, maintainable, and replaceable.

The architecture should faithfully implement the Advisor Intelligence Specification without embedding business logic into infrastructure concerns.

